10. An apparatus for manipulating a position of a substrate, the apparatus comprising:
a support member;
a plurality of support bars coupled to the support member and arrayed to form a parallel rank of support bars;
a first X-Y table coupled to the support member and adapted to translate under motor control in a Y-direction of an X-Y plane;
a second X-Y table coupled to the support member and adapted to translate under motor control in both the Y-direction and an X-direction of the X-Y plane;
a first vacuum gripper coupled to the first X-Y table and controllable in a Z-direction, wherein the first vacuum gripper is adapted to rotate about a Z-axis; and
a second vacuum gripper coupled to the second X-Y table and controllable in the z-direction, wherein the second vacuum gripper is adapted to rotate about the Z-axis.
11. The apparatus of claim 10 wherein an upper surface of the plurality of support bars defines a plane aligned with a lower portion of the substrate.
12. The apparatus of claim 10 wherein the first X-Y table comprises a spring constraining translation of the first X-Y table in the X-direction.
13. The apparatus of claim 10 wherein the first X-Y table and the second X-Y table are adapted to translate a distance greater than 2 meters in the Y-direction.
14. The apparatus of claim 10 wherein at least one of the first vacuum gripper or the second vacuum gripper comprises a gripping surface coupled to a gripper shaft extending into a tandem bearing, wherein the tandem bearing comprises:
a first air bearing characterized by a first diameter;
a second air bearing characterized by a second diameter less than the first diameter.
15. The apparatus of claim 14 wherein the first air bearing and the second air bearing are aligned concentric with a central axis of the tandem bearing.
16. The apparatus of claim 15 wherein the first air bearing is an upper bearing forming a portion of the tandem bearing proximate to the substrate and the second air bearing is a lower bearing forming an opposing portion of the tandem bearing.

17. A vacuum gripper for use in substrate positioning operations, the vacuum gripper comprising:
a vacuum pad adapted to make contact with the substrate;
a shaft connected to the vacuum pad, wherein the shaft is characterized by a first diameter at a portion of the shaft proximal to the vacuum pad and a second diameter at a portion of the shaft distal to the vacuum pad;
a first air bearing surrounding the portion of the shaft proximal to the vacuum pad;
a second air bearing surrounding the portion of the shaft distal to the vacuum pad;
an air source in fluid communication with the first air bearing and the second air bearing;
an exhaust port in fluid communication with the first air bearing and the second air bearing;
a valve in fluid communication with the exhaust port; and
a first flow restrictor in fluid communication with the valve.
18. The vacuum gripper of claim 17 further comprising a second flow restrictor in fluid communication with the valve, wherein the valve is adapted to place either the first flow restrictor or the second flow restrictor in fluid communication with the exhaust port.
19. The vacuum gripper of claim 18 wherein an orifice of the first flow restrictor is characterized by a diameter of different size than an orifice of the second flow restrictor.
20. The vacuum gripper of claim 17 wherein the valve is a solenoid valve.
21. The vacuum gripper of claim 17 wherein the first air bearing is a cylindrical bearing.
22. The vacuum gripper of claim 17 wherein the second air bearing is a cylindrical bearing.
23. The vacuum gripper of claim 17 wherein the first air bearing and the second air bearing comprise a porous material.
